			<item>
				<title>AI Architecture Review Framework</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/review/architecture-review-framework/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/review/architecture-review-framework/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;why-a-review-framework&#34;&gt;Why a review framework&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#why-a-review-framework&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;AI designs fail in predictable places: unclear success criteria, missing permissions in retrieval, agents with too much autonomy, no evaluation, no cost model. A shared framework lets architects, security, risk and product owners review any AI design — your own before you build it, or a team&amp;rsquo;s at an architecture board — consistently and quickly.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Review Questions: Enterprise and Agentic AI</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/review/review-questions/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/review/review-questions/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Answers are deliberately short — enough to check your understanding. Each section links to the article with the full explanation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;aside class=&#34;callout callout--tip&#34; role=&#34;note&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p class=&#34;callout__title&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;callout__label&#34;&gt;Tip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;callout__heading&#34;&gt;How to use this page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;callout__body&#34;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cover the answer, explain it in your own words, then compare. Mark questions you hesitated on and reread the linked article.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/aside&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Enterprise AI Quick Reference</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/review/quick-reference/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/review/quick-reference/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;numbers-to-know&#34;&gt;Numbers to know&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#numbers-to-know&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Item&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Rule of thumb&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Token ↔ text&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;1 token ≈ 4 characters ≈ 0.75 English words; 1,000 tokens ≈ 750 words ≈ 1.5 pages&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Output vs input price&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Output tokens typically cost 3–5× input tokens&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Prompt caching&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Cached input often ~90% cheaper; needs a stable prefix&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Batch APIs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;~50% cheaper; results within hours&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Generation speed&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Tens to a few hundred tokens/s depending on model and load&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Total latency&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;≈ TTFT + output tokens ÷ tokens per second&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Context windows&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;~128K to 1M+ tokens on current frontier models&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Weights memory&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Parameters × bytes per parameter (FP16 = 2, INT8 = 1, INT4 = 0.5); 70B FP16 ≈ 140 GB&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Vector storage&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;vectors × dimensions × 4 bytes (float32); +~50% for HNSW graph&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Chunk size&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;300–800 tokens, 10–20% overlap, plus heading context&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Retrieval&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Retrieve 20–100 candidates → rerank → send 3–8&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Golden dataset&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Start with 50–100 cases, grow to several hundred&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Error compounding&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;0.95 per step over 10 steps ≈ 60% success&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;cost-formula&#34;&gt;Cost formula&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#cost-formula&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;monthly cost = requests/month × (input tokens × input price + output tokens × output price)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;peak TPM     = peak requests/min × (input + output tokens per request)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;prompting-vs-rag-vs-fine-tuning&#34;&gt;Prompting vs RAG vs fine-tuning&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#prompting-vs-rag-vs-fine-tuning&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Need&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Use&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Task definition, format, tone&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Prompting (+ few-shot)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Private, fresh, citable, permissioned knowledge&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;RAG&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Consistent behaviour, domain style, cheaper small model&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Fine-tuning (LoRA)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Actions and live data&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Tools / agents&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;rag-pipeline-at-a-glance&#34;&gt;RAG pipeline at a glance&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#rag-pipeline-at-a-glance&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure class=&#34;diagram&#34; aria-label=&#34;RAG in one line each&#34;&gt;&lt;figcaption class=&#34;diagram__title&#34;&gt;RAG in one line each&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre class=&#34;mermaid&#34;&gt;flowchart LR&#xA;    A[&amp;#34;Load&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; B[&amp;#34;Parse&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; C[&amp;#34;Chunk&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; D[&amp;#34;Enrich + ACL&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; E[&amp;#34;Embed&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; F[(&amp;#34;Index&amp;#34;)]&#xA;    Q[&amp;#34;Query&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; R[&amp;#34;Rewrite&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; S[&amp;#34;Hybrid search + filter&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; T[&amp;#34;Rerank&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; U[&amp;#34;Augment&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; V[&amp;#34;Generate + cite&amp;#34;]&#xA;    F --&amp;gt; S&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Top upgrades by impact:&lt;/strong&gt; parsing &amp;amp; structure-aware chunking → hybrid search → reranking → metadata/ACL filters → query rewriting → contextual retrieval → agentic/graph retrieval.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
	</channel>
